          "text": "## Deliverable\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/li-langverse/lic/pull/176  \n**Branch:** `cursor/compiler-studio-plan-loop` (pushed)\n\n### What changed\n\nPure-Li tier-1 matmul drivers now match the normative C kernels (`reference.py` / `matmul_core.c` / `matmul_blocked_core.c`):\n\n| Bench | Li implementation | Verify checksum (full N) |\n|-------|-------------------|--------------------------|\n| `matmul_naive` | 256×256 IKJ + LUT init | `161055.1865999999` (matches native) |\n| `matmul_blocked` | 512×512 blocked IKJ (BK=64) | `1288460.7563999966` (matches native) |\n\nSupporting work:\n\n- `benchmarks/harness/reference.py` — normative specs\n- `benchmarks/harness/bench.py` — `--verify-results`, Li/native parity via `LI_PRINT_SINK_F64`\n- `runtime/li_rt.c` — print sink when `LI_PRINT_SINK_F64=1`\n- Plan loop scripts + goldens; `wave-a-7e-matmul-pure` marked **completed** in plan YAML\n\n### Tests run\n\n```bash\n./scripts/build.sh\n./scripts/bench-verify-results.sh 1\n./scripts/verify-math-physics-goldens.sh\n./scripts/compiler-studio-plan-gates.sh\npython3 benchmarks/harness/bench.py --tier 1 --runs 3\n./scripts/check-tier1-li-vs-cpp.sh\n```\n\n### Perf honesty (local `latest.csv`, gitignored)\n\n- `matmul_naive`: Li/C++ ≈ **1.0×** (within 1.2× cap)\n- `matmul_blocked`: Li/C++ ≈ **1.96×** (advisory gap — honest pure-Li loops, not DCE)\n\nReplaced the prior tiled `@`-only drivers (wrong init, no checksum parity) with full-size IKJ kernels aligned to the C reference."
