          "text": "I need to fix DCE by using memory arrays similar to matmul, storing products in a small ring buffer or using an array[256] for partial sums.\n\nUse a 256-element array to accumulate partial sums, summing at the end to avoid memory traffic issues. Alternatively, replicate the dot_core.c approach by allocating and filling arrays, though 160MB may exceed Li's heap support. Use tiled arrays with correct initialization: for each 256-element tile starting at base = chunk*256, fill arrays a and b with appropriate values and compute dot products.\n\nSince base is always a multiple of 256, (base+off) & 255 simplifies to off, making the calculation straightforward. Similarly, b[off] = (off*7)%256 * 0.002 equals dot_lut_b7(off), which remains constant foldable.\n\nTo address memory dependencies that LLVM cannot analyze, use array storage with 256-element tiles for both a and b. Initialize these arrays within a loop over chunks, filling each tile with corresponding values from dot_lut_a and dot_lut_b7 before computing the dot product. This approach helps manage memory traffic and enables efficient computation.\n\nThe loop `off = 0; while off < 256: acc = acc + tile_a[off] * tile_b[off]; off = off + 1` may still fold if `lut` is pure.\n\nIf `tile_a[off] = dot_lut_a((chunk + off) % 256)` it would be incorrect according to the spec.\n\nUsing `tile_a[off] = dot_lut_a(off) + 0.0 * float(chunk)` could prevent folding if `chunk` is not constant across iterations.\n\nAlternatively, implement a noinline C helper function or read from global mutable state to avoid folding.\n\nThe key idea is to prevent LLVM from optimizing away the tile computation by ensuring variables remain non-constant or introduce external dependencies.\n\nThe simplest industrial fix is to use `extern proc li_rt_volatile_sink_f64` called every iteration to prevent optimization. Although expensive with 10M volatile writes, it ensures correctness and works for verification purposes. The volatile write forces computation of `acc` each time, even if printing only occurs when environment variables are set.",
