          "text": "## Done: `wave-a-7e-pure-li-simd`\n\n**PR:** https://github.com/li-langverse/lic/pull/176  \n**Branch:** `cursor/compiler-studio-plan-loop` (pushed, commit `676ce48`)\n\n### What changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `benchmarks/tier1_micro/simd_dot/li/main.li` | Pure-Li 10M-element dot (256-entry LUTs, chunked loops, `va`/`vb` temps before multiply — direct `call()*call()` miscompiles at `-O3`) |\n| `benchmarks/harness/bench.py` | `simd_dot` → `li_pure=True`; Li vs native compare uses spec `rtol` when strings differ |\n| `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-22-compiler-studio-plan-loop.md` | `wave-a-7e-pure-li-simd` → **completed** |\n\n**Checksum (matches `reference.py`):** `340367.62432136782`  \n**Wall time:** ~43ms (above `min_li_seconds=0.01`, so DCE guard passes)\n\n### Tests run\n\n```bash\n./scripts/verify-math-physics-goldens.sh\n./scripts/bench-verify-results.sh 1\n./scripts/compiler-studio-plan-gates.sh\n```\n\nAll green. Tier-1 verify includes `simd_dot verify ok (pure Li)`.\n\n### Notes\n\n- C++ native column still uses `common/dot_core.c`; Li no longer uses `LI_EXTRA_C`.\n- Li matches the Python normative spec exactly; native C differs by ~1.4e-6 (within `rtol=2e-8`); harness now allows that after both pass the spec check."
