          "text": "No prior work exists on wave-a-7d-vectorized on this branch.\n\nThe implementation requires wiring `@vectorized` on def to enable array SIMD via decorator, storing `vectorized_lanes` on `MirFn` for codegen. Currently, `@vectorized` does nothing in `apply_fn_decorator_codegen_flags`, only setting `void` lanes. The `enable_array_simd` flag depends on `!fn.no_vectorize`. \n\nMissing features include: `@vectorized` explicitly setting `enable` and storing `lanes` on `MirFn`, and handling conflicts between `@no_vectorize` and `@vectorized` decorators.\n\nThe implementation requires adding `vectorized_lanes` or `array_simd_lanes` to `MirFn` to store lane counts from `@vectorized` decorators, defaulting to 4 when omitted. The `apply_fn_decorator_codegen_flags` function should handle this setting.\n\nThe `@vectorized(lanes=4)` decorator is validated at policy level but doesn't directly control MIR lowering. The `@no_vectorize` decorator disables f644 array SIMD in codegen.\n\nFor wave-a-7d slice, the approach involves:\n1. Adding lane tracking to `MirFn` \n2. Setting `vectorized_lanes` from `@vectorized` decorator\n3. Updating `apply_fn_decorator_codegen_flags` to process these settings\n\nThe default behavior should be OFF unless explicitly enabled by `@vectorized`.",
