            "status": "success",
            "value": {
              "content": "---\ndescription: Competitive HPC intelligence — registry, benches, provability\nglobs:\n  - benchmarks/**/*\n  - compiler/**/simd*\n  - compiler/**/parallel*\n  - docs/benchmarks/**/*\nalwaysApply: false\n---\n\n# Li HPC competitive intelligence\n\nRegistry: `benchmarks/competitive/registry.toml`  \nSkill: `.cursor/skills/hpc-competitive-review/SKILL.md`  \nLandscape: `docs/benchmarks/competitive-landscape.md`\n\n## Before changing benchmarks, SIMD, OpenMP, or tier-2 physics\n\n1. **Read the registry** — confirm `track` (`watch` vs `bench_tier*`) and `kernel_honesty` for each ecosystem.\n2. **Run or refresh benches** — `python3 benchmarks/harness/bench.py --tier 12` (or tier relevant); update `benchmarks/results/latest.csv`.\n3. **Label honesty** — `shared_c_kernel` vs `pure_li` per `benchmarks/results/README.md`; never claim parity on stub kernels.\n4. **No perf claims without evidence** — cite CSV rows + flags; no “faster than Rust” without a reproduced column on the same machine.\n5. **Provability first** — `parallel for` / OpenMP only with discharged Lean contracts; competitor SIMD shortcuts are not license to skip proof.\n\n## Competitive review cadence\n\n- On benchmark/parallel PRs: `./scripts/check-hpc-competitive.sh` (warn-only in v1).\n- Quarterly or on competitor major release: skill workflow — manual release notes, optional `./scripts/hpc-competitive-snapshot.sh`.\n- Stale `last_reviewed` (>90d): update date when reviewed; do not silence warnings without review.\n\n## Gap tracking\n\nWhen a **watch** ecosystem ships a feature Li lacks (e.g. Kokkos team policy, Chapel locale model), file a **G-*** row in the master plan or a short note under `docs/benchmarks/` — do not implement without proof path.\n\n## CI\n\n- PR/main: registry validation is **advisory** (warnings only).\n- Monthly `hpc-competitive` workflow: registry + tier-0 advisory; no competitor network fetch in CI.\n",
              "totalLines": 39,
              "fileSize": 1901
            }
          }
        }
