se/lic/pull/176  \n**Branch:** `cursor/compiler-studio-plan-loop` (pushed at `6bc7514`)\n\n### What changed\n\nTier-2 physics verification was failing because Li drivers did not emit checksums for the harness. This slice:\n\n1. **`verify.py`** — Runs tier-0 compile checks plus tier-2 smokes for `md_lennard_jones` and `heat_equation_2d` (native build, Li build, checksum parity).\n2. **`md_lennard_jones/li/main.li`** — Restored the C-kernel driver (`li_md_kernel` + `li_md_checksum`) with `li_rt_volatile_sink_f64`.\n3. **`heat_equation_2d/li/main.li`** — Same checksum-sink pattern for the PDE smoke.\n4. **`bench.py`** — Dropped `li_pure=True` on MD so it uses the shared `md_core.c` kernel (matches `PERF.md`).\n5. **`compiler-studio-plan-gates.sh`** — Added a tier-2 `verify.py` phase.\n6. **`li-tests/tooling/tier2_physics_verify_smoke.sh`** — Standalone gate script.\n7. **Plan todo** `wave-b-tier2-verify` → **completed**\n\n### Tests run (all green)\n\n```bash\npython3 benchmarks/harness/verify.py\n./scripts/verify-math-physics-goldens.sh\n./scripts/bench-verify-results.sh 1\n./scripts/compiler-studio-plan-gates.sh\n```\n\n### Files touched\n\n- `benchmarks/harness/verify.py`\n- `benchmarks/harness/bench.py`\n- `benchmarks/tier2_physics/md_lennard_jones/li/main.li`\n- `benchmarks/tier2_physics/heat_equation_2d/li/main.li`\n- `scripts/compiler-studio-plan-gates.sh`\n- `li-tests/tooling/tier2_physics_verify_smoke.sh`\n- `docs/release-notes/2026-05-23-wave-b-tier2-verify.md`\n- `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-22-compiler-studio-plan-loop.md`",
    "thinking_text": "The user wants me to implement a code implementer task for the `wave-b-tier2-verify` todo item. I need to understand the requirements for this task before proceeding.The user wants me to implement a code implementer task for the `wave-b-tier2-verify` todo item. I need to understand the requirements for this task before proceeding.First, build lic, then determine what verify.py requires for tier-2 physics.First, build lic, then determine what verify.py requires for tier-2 physics.The task is to make verify.py work with md_lennard_jones and one PDE smoke test, as it currently only supports tier0 sources.The task is to make verify.py work with md_lennard_jones and one PDE smoke test, as it currently only supports tier0 sources.The current verify.py only compiles tier0 Li sources and needs to be updated to handle tier-2 verification.The current verify.py only compiles tier0 Li sources and needs to be updated to handle tier-2 verification.Good, lic is built. Now I will run the tier-2 verification to identify failures and check if verify.py needs extension.Good, lic is built. Now I will run the tier-2 verification to identify failures and check if verify.py needs extension.Need to set CC/CXX to clang-22. Also need to check recent commits and whether verify.py requires extension for tier-2.Need to set CC/CXX to clang-22. Also need to check recent commits and whether verify.py requires extension for tier-2.The task specifically involves verifying that verify.py passes on md_lennard_jones with one PDE smoke test.The task specifically involves verifying that verify.py passes on md_lennard_jones with one PDE smoke test.The md_lennard_jones main.li appears to be a stub and not the actual MD driver.The md_lennard_jones main.li appears to be a stub and not the actual MD driver.The issue is that md_lennard_jones main.li is just a demo stub and not the actual MD kernel.\n\nheat_equation_2d and three_body use extern C kernels but don't sink output. For tier-2 shared C kernel benches, `try_argv_verify=not spec.li_pure` tries `--verify` first for non-pure Li. However, li_main doesn't support `--verify` since it calls extern C kernels directly. The verification logic needs to be handled through the C side instead.The issue is that md_lennard_jones main.li is just a demo stub and not the actual MD kernel.\n\nheat_equation_2d and three_body use extern C kernels but don't sink output. For tier-2 shared C kernel benches, `try_argv_verify=not spec.li_pure` tries `--verify` first for non-pure Li. However, li_main doesn't support `--verify` since it calls extern C kernels directly. The verification logic needs to be handled through the C side instead.The main issues are: 1. `md_lennard_jones/li/main.li` is a stub and requires either a real pure-Li MD implementation or a C kernel call with verify sink.The main issues are: 1. `md_lennard_jones/li/main.li` is a stub and requires either a real pure-Li MD implementation or a C kernel call with verify sink.Interesting - PERF.md indicates that Li links md_core.c through LI_EXTRA_C, whereas bench.py designates md_lennard_jones with `li_pure=True`.\n\nThere's a conflict between PERF.md and bench.py regarding Li's linking approach. The verify task requires running tier-2 verification for md_lennard_jones and heat_equation_2d, but currently fails due to Li drivers not passing verification.\n\nTo resolve this:\n1. Extend verify.py to handle the specified test case\n2. Fix Li drivers to pass verification\n\nFor md_lennard_jones with li_pure=True, either:\n- Implement a pure Li MD version matching native C checksums, or\n- Change li_pure to False to use C kernel as indicated in PERF.md\n\nSince PERF.md shows Li using LI_EXTRA_C, changing li_pure=False in bench.py should align with existing setup.\n\nmain.li should call li_md_kernel and sink the checksum using li_rt_volatile_sink_f64.\n\nHowever, if li_pure=False, the li binary will attempt --verify before execution, but the Li main doesn't parse argv for --verify. Therefore, either add --verify support via argc in Li (if available) or use li_rt_volatile_sink_f64 with li_md_checksum() extern.\n\nFor shared C kernel benches, the pattern is:\n- Declare extern procs for the kernel and checksum\n- Call the kernel in main\n- Sink the checksum using li_rt_volatile_sink_f64\n\nFor `md` with `li_pure=False`, the Li main calls the C kernel and sinks the checksum using `li_rt_volatile_sink_f64`. However, since `md` is marked `li_pure=True`, it should be a pure Li implementation without the C kernel, aligning with the long-term goal of pure Li outperforming C++. \n\nA pragmatic fix for `wave-b-tier2-verify` involves changing `md` to `li_pure=False` to use the C kernel, fixing `heat_equation_2d`'s `main.li`, and extending `verify.py` to support tier-2 smoke tests.Interesting - PERF.md indicates that Li links md_core.c through LI_EXTRA_C, whereas bench.py designates md_lennard_jones with `li_pure=True`.\n\nThere's a conflict between PERF.md and bench.py regarding Li's linking approach. The verify task requires running tier-2 verification for md_lennard_jones and heat_equation_2d, but currently fails due to Li drivers not passing verification.\n\nTo resolve this:\n1. Extend verify.py to handle the specified test case\n2. Fix Li drivers to pass verification\n\nFor md_lennard_jones with li_pure=True, either:\n- Implement a pure Li MD version matching native C checksums, or\n- Change li_pure to False to use C kernel as indicated in PERF.md\n\nSince PERF.md shows Li using LI_EXTRA_C, changing li_pure=False in bench.py should align with existing setup.\n\nmain.li should call li_md_kernel and sink the checksum using li_rt_volatile_sink_f64.\n\nHowever, if li_pure=False, the li binary will attempt --verify before execution, but the Li main doesn't parse argv for --verify. Therefore, either add --verify support via argc in Li (if available) or use li_rt_volatile_sink_f64 with li_md_checksum() extern.\n\nFor shared C kernel benches, the pattern is:\n- Declare extern procs for the kernel and checksum\n- Call the kernel in main\n- Sink the checksum using li_rt_volatile_sink_f64\n\nFor `md` with `li_pure=False`, the Li main calls the C kernel and sinks the checksum using `li_rt_volatile_sink_f64`. However, since `md` is marked `li_pure=True`, it should be a pure Li implementation without the C kernel, aligning with the long-term goal of pure Li outperforming C++. \n\nA pragmatic fix for `wave-b-tier2-verify` involves changing `md` to `li_pure=False` to use the C kernel, fixing `heat_equation_2d`'s `main.li`, and extending `verify.py` to support tier-2 smoke tests.All tier-2 Li drivers require the volatile sink pattern. The task involves md_lennard_jones and one PDE smoke.All tier-2 Li drivers require the volatile sink pattern. The task involves md_lennard_jones and one PDE smoke.The old main.li used li_md_lj_run() with a C kernel, but the li_pure=True flag might be incorrect now that main.li is a stub.The old main.li used li_md_lj_run() with a C kernel, but the li_pure=True flag might be incorrect now that main.li is a stub.None of the tier-2 Li drivers can verify checksums; all require fixes to function properly.\n\nThe task requires running md_lennard_jones and one PDE smoke test. The plan involves fixing the C kernel driver for md_lennard_jones with a volatile sink and adding checksums and volatile sinks to heat_equation_2d. The benchmark file needs to be updated to reflect li_pure=False for md_lennard_jones, and verify.py must be extended to include tier-2 verification for both tests. A check for shared helpers or a dedicated li-tests tier2 directory should also be performed. \n\nThe current approach focuses on ensuring proper checksum handling and volatile sink implementation for these specific tests while maintaining consistency with existing patterns.None of the tier-2 Li drivers can verify checksums; all require fixes to function properly.\n\nThe task requires running md_lennard_jones and one PDE smoke test. The plan involves fixing the C kernel driver for md_lennard_jones with a volatile sink and adding checksums and volatile sinks to heat_equation_2d. The benchmark file needs to be updated to reflect li_pure=False for md_lennard_jones, and verify.py must be extended to include tier-2 verification for both tests. A check for shared helpers or a dedicated li-tests tier2 directory should also be performed. \n\nThe current approach focuses on ensuring proper checksum handling and volatile sink implementation for these specific tests while maintaining consistency with existing patterns.I will read md_energy_single_step.li to determine if verify.py should compile tier0 and run tier2 bench verify.I will read md_energy_single_step.li to determine if verify.py should compile tier0 and run tier2 bench verify.I need to fix `md_lennard_jones/li/main.li` by restoring the C kernel driver with checksum sink.\n\nFix `heat_equation_2d/li/main.li` by adding a checksum sink. Change `li_pure=True` to `li_pure=False` for `md_lennard_jones` in `bench.py` to match PERF.md since we're now using a shared C kernel.\n\nExtend `verify.py` to verify tier-2 md and heat PDE benchmarks using `bench.py`'s verify functions. Consider adding tier-2 verification to `compiler-studio-plan-gates.sh` and `bench-verify-results.sh`. Update the plan YAML todo status and potentially add a `li-tests` script for tier-2 verify smoke tests.\n\nCreate a helper function in `verify.py` to call `bench` verify for specific tier-2 benchmarks and add a `--tier2-smoke` flag or integrate it into `main()` by default.\n\nverify.py currently only performs tier0 compile checks, so I need to extend it for tier-2 verification using bench.py helpers for native+li checksum validation. The extension should include a tier2_smoke_verify function that loops through TIER2_SMOKE benchmarks and uses bench.py's verify functions. I also need to ensure CC=clang-22 is set by having verify.py source llvm-env or set os.en